1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,028
Here's one word, and it shows up in two files, in eight places.

2
00:00:05,928 --> 00:00:08,969
Until now, you've only ever written in one of these files.

3
00:00:09,869 --> 00:00:13,716
So today you'll find out what the other one is doing with your words,

4
00:00:14,166 --> 00:00:16,791
and you'll put two words of your own into both.

5
00:00:18,591 --> 00:00:20,853
Your fact sheet says what the story is,

6
00:00:21,303 --> 00:00:24,977
and this other file, story.mast, is what makes it happen.

7
00:00:25,877 --> 00:00:29,021
And there are five lines in your fact sheet that lean on it.

8
00:00:30,821 --> 00:00:32,486
Scan of derelict is a promise

9
00:00:32,936 --> 00:00:36,216
that something in the game wears the word derelict.

10
00:00:37,116 --> 00:00:40,341
That's called a role, which is really just a name tag.

11
00:00:42,141 --> 00:00:45,187
Done when, signal derelict_found, is a promise too:

12
00:00:45,637 --> 00:00:50,527
that the story will say derelict_found, out loud, at some moment.

13
00:00:51,427 --> 00:00:52,878
And that's called a signal.

14
00:00:54,678 --> 00:00:56,924
If the other file doesn't keep those promises,

15
00:00:57,374 --> 00:00:58,756
the reading is never shown,

16
00:00:59,206 --> 00:01:00,993
and the step never finishes.

17
00:01:02,793 --> 00:01:05,573
So this is story.mast,

18
00:01:06,023 --> 00:01:08,028
and you're not going to learn to read it today.

19
00:01:08,928 --> 00:01:10,231
You only need three rules.

20
00:01:11,131 --> 00:01:14,766
Change only what's between quote marks, or in a note.

21
00:01:15,666 --> 00:01:18,479
Never delete a quote mark, and never add one.

22
00:01:19,379 --> 00:01:22,359
And leave every comma right where it is.

23
00:01:24,159 --> 00:01:27,608
One more thing: a note in this file starts with a hash,

24
00:01:28,058 --> 00:01:31,550
whereas in your fact sheet it starts with two slashes.

25
00:01:33,349 --> 00:01:36,130
Control, shift, F searches the whole folder.

26
00:01:37,030 --> 00:01:39,465
I turn on match case, and match whole word,

27
00:01:39,915 --> 00:01:44,420
so that I get the role itself, and not every word that happens to have it inside.

28
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:46,895
That gives me eight results.

29
00:01:48,695 --> 00:01:50,743
Three of them are my Scan of lines.

30
00:01:51,643 --> 00:01:54,993
The other five are in the story file,

31
00:01:55,443 --> 00:01:58,558
and three of those start with a hash, so they're notes.

32
00:01:59,458 --> 00:02:02,730
That leaves just two lines that do any work.

33
00:02:04,530 --> 00:02:07,284
This first one puts the hulk in the game.

34
00:02:08,184 --> 00:02:10,477
It has four pieces in quotes:

35
00:02:10,927 --> 00:02:13,122
the name the crew sees, then a list,

36
00:02:13,572 --> 00:02:15,851
then the model, and then how it behaves.

37
00:02:16,751 --> 00:02:18,893
The list is the part that's ours.

38
00:02:19,793 --> 00:02:21,376
Its first word is the side,

39
00:02:21,826 --> 00:02:23,921
and every word after that is a role.

40
00:02:24,821 --> 00:02:27,541
So the hulk is on our side, and it wears derelict,

41
00:02:27,991 --> 00:02:29,954
which means that promise is kept.

42
00:02:31,754 --> 00:02:33,364
And here's the word a second time,

43
00:02:33,814 --> 00:02:37,883
in a line that asks: when Science scans something, does it wear derelict?

44
00:02:39,683 --> 00:02:41,327
This search gives me four results.

45
00:02:42,227 --> 00:02:43,784
One is in my fact sheet,

46
00:02:44,234 --> 00:02:45,695
two are in a note,

47
00:02:46,145 --> 00:02:48,353
and one is a working line.

48
00:02:50,153 --> 00:02:53,430
That line has three pieces in quotes,

49
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:56,397
and only the last one is mine.

50
00:02:57,297 --> 00:03:01,013
The first two, quest signal and signal name, are fixed:

51
00:03:01,463 --> 00:03:05,158
touch either of them, and no quest hears anything.

52
00:03:06,058 --> 00:03:09,133
The lines above it decide when the signal is said,

53
00:03:09,583 --> 00:03:12,569
which is when a ship comes within two thousand of the hulk.

54
00:03:13,019 --> 00:03:14,561
I don't need to read those.

55
00:03:16,361 --> 00:03:18,212
The second signal is said down here,

56
00:03:18,662 --> 00:03:20,408
straight under the question about the role.

57
00:03:22,208 --> 00:03:23,766
And one more thing:

58
00:03:24,216 --> 00:03:25,985
a signal is said once,

59
00:03:26,435 --> 00:03:29,742
so a step that hasn't started yet has missed it.

60
00:03:31,542 --> 00:03:33,548
In my story, this hulk is a ghost ship.

61
00:03:34,448 --> 00:03:37,843
And I'm going to do this in the wrong order, on purpose.

62
00:03:38,743 --> 00:03:41,715
First I point my reading at a role that nobody wears.

63
00:03:42,615 --> 00:03:44,305
Lint has read both files,

64
00:03:44,755 --> 00:03:48,680
and it tells me nothing in this mission wears a role called ghost_ship.

65
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:52,177
If I played it now, my reading would simply be gone.

66
00:03:53,977 --> 00:03:56,422
So now I keep the promise, on line sixty-eight.

67
00:03:57,322 --> 00:03:58,972
I click just before the closing quote,

68
00:03:59,422 --> 00:04:04,038
and I type a comma, a space, and the word, and nothing else.

69
00:04:04,938 --> 00:04:07,998
And it's clean, and the hulk wears two roles now.

70
00:04:09,798 --> 00:04:12,278
There are four rules for a role, and they're on the page:

71
00:04:12,728 --> 00:04:14,627
small letters and underscores,

72
00:04:15,077 --> 00:04:17,048
the same spelling in both files,

73
00:04:17,498 --> 00:04:19,347
one thing and not many,

74
00:04:19,797 --> 00:04:21,752
and in a list your word goes last,

75
00:04:22,202 --> 00:04:25,178
because the first word is the side.

76
00:04:26,978 --> 00:04:29,003
Now the same again, with the signal.

77
00:04:29,903 --> 00:04:32,255
My step now waits for ghost_ship_found.

78
00:04:33,155 --> 00:04:35,869
And lint tells me that Find waits for that signal,

79
00:04:36,319 --> 00:04:37,982
and nothing in the mission sends it,

80
00:04:38,432 --> 00:04:39,768
so the wait never ends.

81
00:04:41,568 --> 00:04:43,326
So I search for the old word,

82
00:04:43,776 --> 00:04:47,503
and there are three left, all in the story file.

83
00:04:48,403 --> 00:04:50,033
I do the working line first,

84
00:04:50,483 --> 00:04:52,736
changing the last word in quotes, and only that one.

85
00:04:53,636 --> 00:04:55,235
And now it's clean.

86
00:04:57,035 --> 00:05:00,518
Then I change the note, so that the note stays true,

87
00:05:00,968 --> 00:05:03,499
because lint doesn't read a note, and neither does the game.

88
00:05:05,299 --> 00:05:07,248
And now I count.

89
00:05:08,148 --> 00:05:09,497
The old word gives me nothing,

90
00:05:09,947 --> 00:05:11,906
and the new word gives me four.

91
00:05:13,706 --> 00:05:17,711
Remember that counting, because in two minutes you'll see why it matters.

92
00:05:19,511 --> 00:05:22,700
By now I know every word these two files share,

93
00:05:23,150 --> 00:05:25,410
so I write them down where I'll see them.

94
00:05:26,310 --> 00:05:28,221
That's two roles and two signals,

95
00:05:28,671 --> 00:05:30,628
and where each one comes from.

96
00:05:31,528 --> 00:05:33,474
Every line starts with two slashes,

97
00:05:33,924 --> 00:05:36,755
so the game skips them, and this list is just for me.

98
00:05:38,555 --> 00:05:40,374
When there are thirty of these words,

99
00:05:40,824 --> 00:05:44,154
it's how I'll spell the thirty-first the same way twice.

100
00:05:45,954 --> 00:05:47,070
Now for the honest part.

101
00:05:47,970 --> 00:05:51,396
First, a signal: I misspell it on the working line,

102
00:05:51,846 --> 00:05:55,047
and lint catches it, even though my fact sheet is fine.

103
00:05:55,947 --> 00:05:57,952
That's because for a signal,

104
00:05:58,402 --> 00:06:00,799
lint looks for the line of the story that sends it.

105
00:06:02,599 --> 00:06:05,624
Now a role: I misspell derelict in the hulk's list,

106
00:06:06,074 --> 00:06:07,989
and lint says clean.

107
00:06:08,889 --> 00:06:11,279
And here's why that is.

108
00:06:12,179 --> 00:06:17,535
For a role, lint only looks for the word between quote marks, somewhere in this file,

109
00:06:17,985 --> 00:06:21,829
and it found derelict down here, on line one hundred and three.

110
00:06:22,729 --> 00:06:25,698
It doesn't ask whether the word is in a list of roles.

111
00:06:27,498 --> 00:06:29,906
In the game, the hulk has lost two of its readings,

112
00:06:30,356 --> 00:06:32,718
and the second step never finishes,

113
00:06:33,168 --> 00:06:35,087
and nothing says so.

114
00:06:36,887 --> 00:06:38,513
The count does catch this one:

115
00:06:38,964 --> 00:06:40,890
I get eight, and I wanted nine.

116
00:06:41,790 --> 00:06:43,155
The page lists the rest,

117
00:06:43,605 --> 00:06:47,825
and the two to learn are that your role goes last in the list,

118
00:06:48,275 --> 00:06:50,654
and that it goes after a comma.

119
00:06:52,454 --> 00:06:55,174
The crew never sees a role or a signal.

120
00:06:55,624 --> 00:06:58,012
They only see what those words connect.

121
00:06:58,912 --> 00:07:00,726
So, Find the Derelict is done,

122
00:07:01,176 --> 00:07:02,227
and that was my signal:

123
00:07:02,677 --> 00:07:06,709
the story said ghost_ship_found, and my step was waiting for it.

124
00:07:07,609 --> 00:07:10,086
The sensors scan the hulk by themselves,

125
00:07:10,536 --> 00:07:12,534
so the second step finishes too.

126
00:07:14,334 --> 00:07:16,789
And on Science there are three tabs,

127
00:07:17,239 --> 00:07:20,187
and intel is the one that's hanging on my role.

128
00:07:21,087 --> 00:07:22,836
And both logs are empty.

129
00:07:24,636 --> 00:07:26,502
Now it's time for your own words.

130
00:07:27,402 --> 00:07:28,943
Give the station a role,

131
00:07:29,393 --> 00:07:32,057
and a reading on its mat tab.

132
00:07:32,957 --> 00:07:35,692
Then rename the second signal, in both files,

133
00:07:36,142 --> 00:07:37,991
and add both to your list.

134
00:07:39,791 --> 00:07:41,508
Next time it's your first quest:

135
00:07:41,958 --> 00:07:43,570
a line that names a role,

136
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:46,694
and the game does the watching itself.
